    notes: Source-qualified stock identity with partial literal component assertion.
      DSMZ878 defines the reagent as 0.01 M Fe citrate stock and adds 0.5 ml. The
      flattened g/L discrepancy belongs to the receiving-medium transcription. A partial
      source-qualified stock can retain 0.01 M literally while leaving iron valence,
      citrate ratio and solvent ungrounded. Stock solute oxidation state/ligand ratio
      and solvent remain unspecified; no mass conversion or molecular exact identity
      is authorized.
